cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "A Lean 4 Formalization of Interpreting Lambda Calculus in Domain-Valued Random Variables (CSL 2026)"
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ericson
    given-names: Lars Warren
    affiliation: Catskills Research Company
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8299-9361"
abstract: >-
  Sorry-free Lean 4 / mathlib formalization of Furber, Mardare, Panangaden, and
  Scott's Interpreting Lambda Calculus in Domain-Valued Random Variables
  (LIPIcs, CSL 2026). Covers every numbered paper item from Theorem 1 through
  Proposition 44, including the internal Engeler model, Theorems 26 and 30,
  Corollary 34, and Theorem 43 (incomparable λ-degrees of two fair-coin
  subsets of ℕ). The paper's authors were not contacted and did not
  participate in, review, or endorse this formalization.
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - domain theory
  - lambda calculus
  - denotational semantics
  - probabilistic programming
  - Boolean-valued models
  - formal verification
